  DetailImage: {fileID: 0}
  DetailText: "* Greek Letters*\n\nTranslation:\nMany were the men whose cities he
    saw and whose mind he learned, aye, and many the woes he suffered in his heart
    upon the sea, seeking to win his own life and the return of his comrades. Yet
    even so he saved not his comrades, though he desired it sore, for through their
    own blind folly they perished\u2014fools, who devoured the kine of Helios Hyperion;
    but he took from them the day of their returning. Of these things, goddess, daughter
    of Zeus, beginning where thou wilt, tell thou even unto us."
